2. The Narrative Ontology

Pantheon can distinguish several major narrative objects.

\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
Archetype &= \text{stable attractor}\\
Role &= \text{temporary policy binding}\\
Trope &= \text{compressed causal transformation}\\
Motif &= \text{recurrent semantic feature}\\
PlotDevice &= \text{state-transition mechanism}\\
Plotline &= \text{trajectory family}\\
Scene &= \text{local transition window}\\
Conflict &= \text{gradient / incompatible objectives}\\
Symbol &= \text{high-density semantic address}\\
Theme &= \text{persistent evaluative invariant}\\
Kata &= \text{demonstration trajectory}\\
Story &= \text{composed state evolution}
\end{aligned}
}

These are not synonyms.

They occupy different layers of the narrative machine.

