5. Archetypes as Policy Priors

The important move:

An archetype can be temporarily bound to an interpreter.

Interpreter
+
Archetype
\rightarrow
PolicyPrior

Example:

WITH_ARCHETYPE("Mentor"):
    solve(problem)

does not mean:

Pretend literally to be a mythical mentor.

It means:

Weight actions toward capability transfer, demonstration, learner independence, and scaffolding.

Thus archetypes become policy lenses.

They are not identities that must permanently consume the actor.

They are temporary programs.

