8. Plotlines — Trajectory Families

A plotline is not merely a sequence of events.

It is a class of trajectories sharing causal topology.

Define:

P=
(N_0,T_1,T_2,...,T_n,N_n)

Two stories can share a plotline even if every surface detail differs.

Therefore:

\boxed{
Plotline =
equivalence class of narrative trajectories
}

where equivalence is defined over meaningful state transitions rather than scenery.

