General topology:

Home
\rightarrow
Objective
\rightarrow
Departure
\rightarrow
Obstacles
\rightarrow
Transformation
\rightarrow
Acquisition
\rightarrow
Return

Mathematically:

\pi^*
=
\arg\min_{\pi}
Cost(\pi)

subject to:

GoalReached(\pi)=1.

But a meaningful quest usually changes the traveler:

Agent_{return}
\neq
Agent_{departure}.

So:

QUEST
=
PathPlanning
+
ObstacleAdaptation
+
IdentityDelta

QUEST(
    agent,
    objective,
    unknown_space
)
→ route
→ trials
→ adaptation
→ objective_result
→ changed_agent

This maps directly to Scout → Route → Exercise → Delta → Return.

