32. The Character Arc

A character arc can be modeled as a trajectory in identity-policy space.

Let:

C_t=(Beliefs,Values,Capabilities,Relationships,Policy).

Then:

Arc=
C_0
\rightarrow
C_1
\rightarrow
...
\rightarrow
C_n.

The meaningful quantity is:

\Delta C=C_n-C_0.

A flat arc intentionally has:

\Delta C\approx0

while the character instead transforms the environment.

This distinction matters.

Not every protagonist must internally mutate.

Sometimes the stable invariant is the causal force.

